8 #edb/ref 17592186101616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101614 #edb/ref 1061 1253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101614 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6a979657-a144-5dbc-997b-c1dd2371aada" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101614 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186102007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101615 #edb/ref 1061 1254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101615 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f59c1bb5-ff3b-5994-8b51-510587d9b7d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101615 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101616 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101616 #edb/ref 1061 1257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101616 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "049dcac4-b6ea-586e-a449-913e4b288153" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101616 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101784 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101784 #edb/ref 1061 26716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101784 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "21d8a180-a349-5a05-bcdf-9edbed0ff759" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101784 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102007 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we want to sketch a possible graph of a function $f(x)$ that satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- $f'(3)=0$\n- if $x \\in (-\\infty,3)$ then $f'(x)> 0$\n- if $x \\in (3,+\\infty)$ then $f'(x)<0$\n- $f''(x) < 0$ for all $x \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$\n\nWe summarize all the given information in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty,3)$ | $3$ | $(3,\\infty)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f'$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f''$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $\\nearrow\\:\\:\\frown$ | $\\textrm{max}$ | $\\searrow\\:\\:\\frown$ |\n\nNow, let's sketch our graph:\n\n- We draw a point on the vertical line $x=3$, where the tangent to the graph is horizontal.\n- Since $x=3$ is a local maximum, the graph must go down to the left and to the right of that point.\n- Finally, the graph must be concave down everywhere.\n\nTherefore, a possible graph of $f$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/7c/7c6d8412e9c657e8e4a148e40ca0b8a073735d3b88681eec6a79f763471aaf4f.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102007 #edb/ref 1065 655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102007 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7f1b863e-e172-5e84-8f8d-1ea21025605d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102007 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
